  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Georgia received $263M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. AwardCount reached 3,795 and averageAwardSize was $69.2K. Obligations fell 97.4% year over year compared with prior full fiscal years, reflecting that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Previous fiscal years show materially larger totals, including FY26 at $10.3B, FY25 at $12B, FY24 at $10.7B, FY23 at $11.5B, and FY22 at $8.9B. The Department of Health and Human Services led buying in FY2027 to date, obligating $116M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $67.7M and the Department of Homeland Security at $29.6M. FOUR SEASONS ENVIRONMENTAL INC received the largest vendor total, with $51.9M in obligations. Facilities Support Services was the largest industry by obligations at $54.5M, with Security Guards and Patrol Services at $25.7M and Janitorial Services at $18.7M also prominent. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date activity for FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the largest buyers in Georgia?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $116M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $67.7M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $29.6M. The Department of Justice, Department of Labor, and Department of Agriculture followed with $13.3M, $11.4M, and $9.9M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and which industries draw the most spending?",
        "body": "FOUR SEASONS ENVIRONMENTAL INC received $51.9M in obligations, the largest vendor total in FY2027 to date. T47 INTERNATIONAL, INC. and XPRESTEST INC. received $18.7M and $16.7M respectively. Facilities Support Services led industries with $54.5M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $25.7M and Janitorial Services at $18.7M."
      }
